    "sourceGaps": [
      "2008E3: This attributed 2009 Sirota/IUVENTA archive compilation prints the question and a complete connected key. The question promises a solubility table on the next page, but that question resource is absent here; the printed key's observation matrix is a different table. No missing table or experimental observation is invented. The key adds phosphate to the possible-anion list although phosphate is absent from the question list. Its first lead-acetate formula is malformed, while the following Pb(OAc)₂ abbreviation is printed normally. The matrix retains clipped “odourles” cells. The printed “2+4 form either a precipitate or ammonia” disagrees with the matrix's “no change” cell and is retained literally. Although the initial sample list gives AgNO₃, the final reasoning leaves its anion as nitrate or perchlorate, consistent with the question's permission to give the narrowest selection. The eight tubes remain one connected practical problem, not eight separate assignments.\n\nEditable working transcription from native physical Q726 and K727–730, exact inherited726–727 at zero fresh credit; actual fresh728–733 original six-page checkpoint. Common appendix731–733 is retained separately with exact printed units/constants/symbols. No independent checker or new source-reading credit during construction; ROOT alone promotes/publishes."
